    question: 'Should I use Udemy or my own platform?',
    answer: '<p><strong>Use Udemy if:</strong> You have no existing audience, want marketplace discovery, and are okay with lower per-sale revenue. Udemy\'s 57 million students can discover your course, but you keep only 37% of sales they generate.</p><p><strong>Use your own platform if:</strong> You have an audience (email list, social following), want to build a brand, and keep more revenue. Platforms like Teachable let you keep 95-100% of sales.</p><p>Many creators do both: use Udemy for discovery and their own platform for premium courses with higher prices.</p>'
